/* Size probes.

   Four entry points over the same application shell, differing only in how much of the library
   they import. `pnpm check:dist` builds all four and compares their gzip sizes, so "what does an
   application pay" is a measurement rather than the size of the FESM files we ship.

   `paths` is repeated here rather than in the root tsconfig because the library source is mapped
   there for the demo. The probe must measure the **built package** instead: the shipped FESM is
   what an application installs, and Angular's compiler plus `sideEffects: false` are part of what
   makes unused parts disappear. Build the library before building a probe. Type-aware ESLint reads
   this file too, so `pnpm verify` and CI build the library before linting. */
{
  "extends": "../../tsconfig.json",
  "compilerOptions": {
    "outDir": "../../out-tsc/probe",
    "types": [],
    "paths": {
      "ng-signal-request": ["../../dist/signal-request"],
      "ng-signal-request/devtools": ["../../dist/signal-request/devtools"],
      "ng-signal-request/persist": ["../../dist/signal-request/persist"]
    }
  },
  "files": [],
  "include": ["src/**/*.ts"]
}
